{"abstain":false,"answer":"The greenhouse effect involves the atmosphere holding onto heat rather than letting it escape into space. The document explains that if the atmosphere holds onto too much heat at night, the Sun heats Earth’s surface even more the next day. [S1]

If this greenhouse effect works too strongly, Earth gets progressively warmer, although the change may not be measurable from day to day or even year to year. [S2]

So, the document describes a potentially harmful effect when too much heat is trapped. However, the provided excerpts do not explain whether the greenhouse effect at normal levels is beneficial.","citations":["S1","S2"]}
